// http_host/mod.d.rut — the std HTTP surface's root: a `type =
// "host"` pkg whose root surface is this file (the default root —
// `mod.d.rut` beside the manifest, lib parity with a body's
// `mod.rut`) and whose surface organizes as a MODULE TREE (the
// host-.d.rut-mod-tree plan's pilot). The root declares the two lanes
// — `net` (the request lane and the response readbacks) and `stream`
// (the body lanes) — whose rows live in `net/mod.d.rut` and
// `stream/mod.d.rut` beside this file. The rows register
// path-qualified (`http_host::net::http_send__start` et al); the
// embedding Rust binds them through the pkg scope
// (`HostPkg::new("http_host")` + `"net::http_send"`).
//
// The bodies live in rut-std (`http::pkg_with` — the fixture lane —
// and `http::pkg()`, the reqwest lane); the async rows expand into
// their row families (`__start`/`__yield`/`__take`/`__cancel` — the
// host future lane) and ride `register_async!` at the embedder.
// `rut/http` (the class face) imports through the qualified spellings
// (`use http_host::net::{ .. }`, `use http_host::stream::{ .. }`).

pub mod net;
pub mod stream;
